# Simplified Prose Demo - New Features

# --- Implicit variable declaration ---
# No need for "A Number named X exists." - just assign!
X is 42.
Print "X = ${X}".

Name is "Prose".
Print "Hello, ${Name}!".

# --- Map: transform every item ---
To double a Number:
    Result is Number times 2.

A List named Numbers exists.
Numbers contains 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5.

A List named Doubled exists.
Doubled is every item in Numbers transformed by double.
Print "Doubled: " followed by Doubled.

# --- Filter: keep items where condition ---
A List named Big exists.
Big is every item in Numbers where _item is greater than 2.
Print "Big: " followed by Big.

# --- Sum ---
A Number named Total exists.
Total is the sum of Numbers.
Print "Sum: " followed by Total.

# --- Whenever on plain variable ---
Whenever X changes:
    Print "X changed to ${X}!".

X is 100.

# --- File ops ---
Write "test data" to the file "test_simplify.txt".
Print "File written".

A Text named ReadBack exists.
Read the file "test_simplify.txt" into ReadBack.
Print "Read: " followed by ReadBack.

Delete the file "test_simplify.txt".
Print "File deleted".

# --- List directory ---
A List named DirFiles exists.
DirFiles is the list of files in ".".
Print "Files in current dir: " followed by DirFiles.
